Approved subject to the following conditions:
1. That the front porch have a minimum depth of 6 feet, include a two-step elevation,
and utilize 8" x 8" columns, with a design that reflects the traditional architectural
character of the blockface;
2. That the proposed front door be modified to a solid or minimal traditional-style door
compatible with the historic context;
3. That additional single or paired 1/1 windows be provided on the front-facing portions
of both the left and right elevations, and that all paired windows include a 4-inch
mullion;
4. That the siding reveal be specified as 6 inches;
5. That a dimensioned contextual site plan be submitted demonstrating compliance with
the existing buildable setbacks;
6. That complete information regarding the driveway materials and total paving area be
provided, consistent with the Guidelines.
7. That any adjustments made to the drawings be submitted to the Development
Services Department prior to the issuance of a Certificate of Appropriateness.
